Add a windows-x86_64 target linked by the MinGW flavour of lld

The toolchain names x86_64-w64-mingw32, with mingw as its libc and ABI
so rules_cc can recognise the target. lld takes none of the ELF link
flags for it, as for wasm, so they are skipped, and its MinGW flavour
has no --start-lib, so archives are linked whole. A MinGW sysroot keeps
its headers, libstdc++'s included, under /include, and the GCC runtime
under /lib/gcc, so those are the builtin include directories.

